WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.184
(relaxed music)

00:00:03.184 --> 00:00:04.612
- [Narrator] For six months of the year,

00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:07.037
crystal blue lagoons appear
in what would otherwise

00:00:07.037 --> 00:00:10.017
look like your average desert,

00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:12.042
making Lençóis Maranhenses

00:00:12.042 --> 00:00:15.792
one of Brazil's most
mysterious destinations.

00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:25.163
Lençóis Maranhenses is a
national park located in Brazil.

00:00:25.163 --> 00:00:27.281
From January to June, the area

00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:30.967
becomes inundated with rain storms.

00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:33.290
The rain water collects
between the sand dunes,

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.184
creating thousands of clear water lagoons.

00:00:37.184 --> 00:00:40.408
Some of these pools reach
over 300 feet in length

00:00:40.408 --> 00:00:42.825
and can be over 10 feet deep.

00:00:43.669 --> 00:00:46.776
With water temperatures
as high as 87 degrees,

00:00:46.776 --> 00:00:48.292
visitors come from far and wide

00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:52.226
to experience the pristine conditions.

00:00:52.226 --> 00:00:54.727
But arriving at these
pools is no easy feat,

00:00:54.727 --> 00:00:56.848
and renting a four-wheeler is a must.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:59.285
The ride is rough, as you
need to cross tight spaces

00:00:59.285 --> 00:01:03.175
and navigate through rivers and puddles.

00:01:03.175 --> 00:01:05.764
Lençóis Maranhenses visitors
must enjoy these pools

00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:08.928
while they can, because come dry season

00:01:08.928 --> 00:01:11.319
this spectacular landscape vanishes

00:01:11.319 --> 00:01:14.819
and returns to its desert form once again.

